    "updated_at": "2023-10-29T08:51:54Z",
    "body": "Thanks for your question. The condition column just refers to the gene that is perturbed within each cell. It is usually provided in the `.obs` metadata within the `AnnData` object.\r\n\r\nAre you using this [link](https://plus.figshare.com/articles/dataset/_Mapping_information-rich_genotype-phenotype_landscapes_with_genome-scale_Perturb-seq_Replogle_et_al_2022_processed_Perturb-seq_datasets/20029387) to download the Replogle 2022 (Cell) dataset?\r\n\r\nIf so, you will find the condition variable under the `gene` column in `adata.obs` for any of the anndata files that are provided on that webpage.\r\n\r\n```\r\n      cell_barcode      gem_group   gene          gene_id  ...                                                  \r\n AAACCCAAGAAATCCA-27         27     NAF1  ENSG00000145414  ...      \r\n AAACCCAAGAACTTCC-31         31     BUB1  ENSG00000169679  ...      \r\n```\r\n\r\nFollowing this the standard GEARS preprocessing is to just convert this column to the format `<perturbed gene>+ctrl` for single-gene perturbations.\r\n\r\nLet me know if you have any other questions.\r\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
